



Reasoning models need some form of recurrence; they need a way to refer to and reason over previous thoughts or results.

Article on test-time computes covers many methods that use recurrence. Let's discuss broad categories / tools.

Define recurrence as repeated operations over a value, to improve quality of output.

Internal recurrence, architectural recurrence (RNN, LPN, CTM)
Reccurence over intermediares / iterative refinement (EBM, Diffusion)
Recurrence over outputs, auto-regressive, prompt-recurrence (LLMs, CoT, ReAct)
Recurrence over variables, explicit memory, symbolic or structured latent variables (NSM, Pointer networks; program synthesis?, Neural Turing Machines?)


Recurrence over environment


Combinations: Transformer-XL (internal + outputs)